.SH NAME
CWE\-778 \- Insufficient Logging
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
When a security\-critical event occurs, the product either does not record the event or omits important details about the event when logging it. When security\-critical events are not logged properly, such as a failed login attempt, this can make malicious behavior more difficult to detect and may hinder forensic analysis after an attack succeeds. As organizations adopt cloud storage resources, these technologies often require configuration changes to enable detailed logging information, since detailed logging can incur additional costs. This could lead to telemetry gaps in critical audit logs. For example, in Azure, the default value for logging is disabled.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2026\-41709
Broadcom VMware ESX, added 2026\-10\-28.
.PP
Broadcom VMWare ESX Insufficient Logging Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Broadcom VMWare ESX contains an insufficient logging vulnerability that could allow a malicious actor with admin access to perform certain operations without being logged.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply vendor mitigations; follow CISA BOD 26\-04 (risk\-based patching) and forensics triage. Discontinue use if no mitigation exists.
 Due 2026\-11\-11.
.PP
